          "styling_eyebrow": "How to Wear",
          "styling_title": "Four ways to wear a square",
          "styling_intro": "<p>One square of silk is never only one thing. These are the four we return to most — each takes under a minute, and none of them need a pin.</p>",
          "styling_1_name": "The Neck Knot",
          "styling_1_text": "Fold the square corner to corner, then roll it down into a soft band. Wrap once around the neck and tie a loose knot off to one side. Leave the tails uneven — it reads more relaxed than a centred bow.",
          "styling_2_name": "The Bandeau",
          "styling_2_text": "Fold to a band roughly two fingers wide. Lay it across the crown of the head and tie at the nape, underneath the hair. Tuck the ends up and out of sight for a clean line.",
          "styling_3_name": "The Handle Wrap",
          "styling_3_text": "Fold into a narrow strip and wind it around the base of a bag handle, overlapping as you go. Finish with a small knot and let one tail fall. It softens a hard handle and carries colour where you need it.",
          "styling_4_name": "The Shoulder Drape",
          "styling_4_text": "Open the square fully and lay it flat across one shoulder, points falling front and back. Belt it at the waist over a plain shirt or fine knit. The quietest way to wear the whole print.",
